    "rootCauseMd": "The change replaces `zone_for(zone).localize(moment)` with `moment.replace(tzinfo=zone_for(zone))` on the lines marked by the diff (`moment = zone_for(zone).localize(moment)` \u2192 `moment = moment.replace(tzinfo=zone_for(zone))`). `replace` merely attaches the zone\u2019s tzinfo object without applying the zone\u2019s historical offset rules for that date, so the naive midnight is interpreted using the zone\u2019s raw offset (which includes a non\u2011standard minute component for America/Mexico_City) instead of being properly localized, producing 06:37 UTC rather than the expected 06:00 UTC. Restoring the original `localize` call (or using `zone_for(zone).localize(moment)`) fixes the test."
  },
